    "lyrics": {
      "text": "Ne. Glo---ry to the Fa-ther, and to___ the__ Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir----it.\n\nThe tast--ing of the___ tree__ be-came a source__ of__ an---guish for Ad-am in E-den__ in___ time__ past, when the ser----pent__ dis-charged his ven----om. For by__ him death__ en--tered____ in, de-vour-ing the___ whole race__ of____ man. But when the__ Mas-ter__ came, He de-stroyed the drag----on and grant---ed res-ur-rec--tion un--to___ us. There-fore, let us cry____ un---to___ Him:__ O Sav-iour, spare___ those whom Thou hast tak-en__ to____ Thy--self_____________ and grant them__ rest_____ with__ the right---eous.__\n\nBoth now and ev---er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nThe trans-for-ma-tion of the af-flict--ed and the re-lief of those in sick--ness art thou in truth, O Vir-gin The-o-to-kos; save thy peo-ple and thy flock, thou who art the peace of the em-bat--tled, and who art the calm of the__ storm-driv-en, the on-ly pro-tec-tress of those who be-lieve.___"
    }
